  "explanation": {
    "short": "Now you can read a Thai syllable like a puzzle: find the class of the first letter, see whether the syllable is live or dead, then look for a tone mark. A mark always beats the plain rule, and ์ above a letter means that letter is silent (โบสถ์ is \"bot\").",
    "more": "Quick table. No mark, live: mid class mid, high class rising, low class mid. No mark, dead: mid class low, high class low, low class high (short) or falling (long). With ่: mid low, high low, low falling. With ้: mid falling, high falling, low high. The rare marks ๊ and ๋ only appear on mid-class letters and give high and rising: โต๊ะ is high. A tone is a property of the whole syllable, so a word with two syllables has two tones: ถนน, สบาย. You will need this table less and less: after enough Thai you simply know the tone of each word."
  },
